'''''Ceropegia linearis''''', also known as '''string-of-needles''',{{cn|date=October 2024}} is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[family (botany)|family]] [[Apocynaceae]], native to Southern Africa.<ref name=POWO>{{cite taxon |POWO |id=95645-1 |title=''Ceropegia linearis'' E.Mey. |access-date=June 20, 2026}}</ref><ref name=COL>{{Catalogue of Life |id=32NCZ |title=''Ceropegia linearis'' E.Mey. |access-date=June 20, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ville-ge.ch/musinfo/bd/cjb/africa/details.php?langue=an&id=175781 |title=African Plant Database |publisher=[[Conservatory and Botanical Garden of the City of Geneva|Les Conservatoire et Jardin Botaniques de la Ville de Genève]] |accessdate=7 July 2014}}</ref> The popular houseplant ''[[Ceropegia woodii]]'' is sometimes treated as a [[subspecies]] of ''C. linearis'', as ''C. linearis'' subsp. ''woodii''.<ref name=POWO/> It has gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref name = RHSPF>{{cite web 
| url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/74288/Ceropegia-linearis-subsp-woodii/Details | title = ''Ceropegia linearis'' subsp. ''woodii''
| website = www.rhs.org | publisher = Royal Horticultural Society | accessdate = 12 April 2020}}</ref> 

